A table goes on purpose, and a trigger still writes it. SQLite would make
the trigger and fail at the first write that fires it; roux-db compiles
every trigger, so the build says it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE log (what TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TRIGGER logged AFTER INSERT ON dish BEGIN INSERT INTO log (what) VALUES (new.name); END;
INSERT INTO dish (name) VALUES ('soup');

== after
-- @drop table log
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TRIGGER logged AFTER INSERT ON dish BEGIN INSERT INTO log (what) VALUES (new.name); END;

== error
roux-db: trigger logged: no such table: main.log (where an INSERT on dish fires it)
